  "description": "The western becomes a storybook that keeps turning lethal. Six chapters from a singing gunslinger to a stagecoach of the dead, framed as pages of an old cloth-bound book — tonal whiplash as structure: farce, then a prospector's idyll, then the bleakest thing the Coens have made. The genre sampled across its whole emotional range in one sitting.\n\nSix tales of life and violence in the Old West, following a singing gunslinger, a bank robber, a traveling impresario, an elderly prospector, a wagon train and a perverse pair of bounty hunters.",
